Version 3.0.0 (2026-10-07)
==========================

Rewritten in Rust; speaks sway/i3 IPC directly.

- Fixed the focused window being sent to the scratchpad instead of the launched app:
  subscribe to window events before launching, only accept `new` windows, identify the
  window by process ancestry, and mark that exact container
- Fallback for single-instance apps that open their window from an existing process
- New --app-id / --class options to identify the window explicitly
- New --timeout option (default raised from 2 s to 5 s)
- Concurrent invocations for the same command no longer launch duplicate instances
- Slide animations and -s now use absolute coordinates, fixing multi-monitor placement
- -w now takes its argument as documented
- Same flags and window marks as 2.x: existing bindings and windows keep working

Versions up to 2.2: see https://github.com/emilyyyylime/sway-scratchpad
